{"id":"word:hebrew:H577","type":"word","title":"אָנָּא","subtitle":"H577 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"oh now!","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to אָנָּא (H577) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: inj.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 13 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"אָנָּא (ʼânnâʼ) means oh now! First listed occurrence: 2Kgs 20 3."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"אָנָּא","transliteration":"ʼânnâʼ","pronunciation":"awn-naw'","strong":"H577","lemmaId":"hebrew:H577","partOfSpeech":"inj","forms":["אָנָּ֤ה","אָנָּ֣א","אָנָּ֣ה","אָנָּ֤א","אָ֣נָּ֗א"],"morphs":[["HTe",7],["HTj",6]]},"definitions":{"short":"oh now!","usage":"I (me) beseech (pray) thee, O.","full":"H577. annah or anna אָֽנָּ֫א interjection (from אָהּ and נָא , q. v.) a strong particle of entreaty, ah, now! I (or We) beseech thee! often followed by an imperative; Gen 50:17 (to Joseph) וג נָא שָׂא ׳אָנָּא Ah, now ! forgive, we pray, etc., Exod 32:31 (to God); elsewhere always followed by ׳י or אֲדֹנָי Psa 118:25 (twice in verse); Neh 1:5 , 11 ; Dan 9:4 . Written אָֽנָּ֫ה 2Kin 20:3 (= Isa 38:3 ) Jonah 1:14 ; 4:2 ; Psa 116:4 ; 116:16 . אנב (perhaps spring, leap , so Dl HA 65, Pr 114 , inferred from Assyrian annabu , hare ; against this Nö ZMG 1886, 734 ).","rootNote":"or אָנָּה ; apparent contracted from 160 and 4994 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"2Kgs 20 3","keyReferences":["2Kgs 20 3","Dan 9 4","Exod 32 31","Gen 50 17","Isa 38 3","Jonah 1 14","Jonah 4 2","Neh 1 5"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":13,"occurrences":[{"reference":"2Kgs 20 3","book":"2Kgs","chapter":20,"verse":3,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אָנָּ֣ה","source":"hebrew","morph":"HTj"},{"reference":"Dan 9 4","book":"Dan","chapter":9,"verse":4,"englishText":"","sourceWord":"אָנָּ֤א","source":"hebrew","mor